          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000029\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"A gentle, coherent invitation succeeds when Pip settles on the ribbon; the silver-dust image gives it a concrete close, though the conflict is slight.\"},{\"id\":\"s000057\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The softened lamp usefully supports the shy moth’s arrival, and the ending is vivid; some repeated setup and action slow the small story.\"},{\"id\":\"s000047\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Ada and Bo deliberately make the display quiet, Pip approaches, and the final shadow completes the scene; it is polished but lightly plotted.\"},{\"id\":\"s000073\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The still moon tableau gives Pip a calm reason to land, with a clear visual ending; the story has little obstacle beyond Pip’s initial shyness.\"},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Ada notices Pip is small, tries an overly bright shadow show, and begins adapting; the moth remains frightened, making the question-like ending emotionally coherent but incomplete.\"},{\"id\":\"s000043\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The quiet tableau leads directly to Pip settling on the ribbon, and the moth’s shadow provides a satisfying concrete final image.\"},{\"id\":\"s000068\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Bo’s moonflower scent gently draws Pip to the blossoms, ending in a pleasing dew-drop image; it reads more as a calm visit than a developed problem-and-turn story.\"},{\"id\":\"s000096\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The paper-moon performance and ribbon culminate clearly in Pip’s landing; the action order is slightly awkward because the ribbon is tied after the tableau begins.\"},{\"id\":\"s000005\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Moonflower scent brings Pip safely to the garden, with strong sensory details and a concrete close, but little consequential change or challenge.\"},{\"id\":\"s000085\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":9,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Ada discovers that her grand plan would scare Pip, changes it to a quiet tableau, and Pip arrives; this has the clearest state-driven turn and a lovely final image.\"}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":3,\"causal_path\":4,\"ending\":3,\"language\":4,\"overall\":3},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All stories share Ada and Bo inviting shy moth Pip into the moonlit garden. Most use the same quiet paper-moon/ribbon approach and identical landing image (s000029, s000043, s000047, s000057, s000073, s000096, s000085). The moonflower-scent path in s000005 and s000068 is a modest alternate route, while s000034 ends with Pip still startled rather than welcomed. This sample does not establish diversity across the entire generator.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"story_ids\":[\"s000029\",\"s000057\",\"s000047\",\"s000073\",\"s000043\",\"s000096\"],\"summary\":\"Ada and Bo create a quiet paper-moon welcome; Pip approaches and rests on the ribbon, completing the invitation.\"},{\"story_ids\":[\"s000085\"],\"summary\":\"Ada learns Pip is hiding because a grand show would be too much, changes to a still tableau, and Pip comes to the ribbon.\"},{\"story_ids\":[\"s000034\"],\"summary\":\"Ada discovers Pip’s shyness and attempts a bright shadow show; Pip is startled and hides, leaving the welcome unresolved.\"},{\"story_ids\":[\"s000068\",\"s000005\"],\"summary\":\"Bo uses the scent of moonflowers as a gentle invitation; Pip lands among the blossoms for a calm visit.\"}]}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
